Submission guidelines
The submission deadline for the group presentation is on Friday 12th December 2025 (Week 10) at 16:00. Unapproved late submissions will be penalised.
Each group should prepare two files: a PDF/PPT copy of the presentation file and a video recording of the presentation in MP4 format.
The name of the presentation file should be the capitalised name of your group followed by “_presentation”, for example “FANTASTIC_SIX_presentation.pdf” or “FANTASTIC_SIX_presentation.ppt”, depending on the file type.
Similarly, the name of the video recording should be the capitalised name of your group followed by "_video", for example "FANTASTIC_SIX_video.mp4".
The presentation should be no longer than 10 minutes. It is the group’s choice as to how many members will appear in the video.
Moodle poses a restriction on the aggregate size of the submission files: the sum of the sizes of the submitted files should not exceed 100 MB. For this reason, the spokesperson / representative of each group should:
upload both the PDF/PPT presentation file and the MP4 file on Moodle (as two separate files) if their combined size is smaller than or equal to 100 MB.
upload the PDF/PPT presentation file on Moodle and upload the MP4 file on the "Files" section of the group's private Teams channel, if their combined size is larger than 100 MB. Please include a link to the MP4 file in the PDF/PPT presentation.
Marking Scheme (25 marks)
Appropriate presentation format and delivery [5 marks]
Introduction, background and strategy [6 marks]
Articulation of the project's brief and motivation
Explanation of the research question and objectives
Research strategy, software tools and team collaboration
Data pre-processing and analysis [7 marks]
Explanation and justification of appropriate data processing and integration
Explanation / rationale of the data analysis techniques used (machine learning, statistical models)
Research outcomes [7 marks]
Analysis of the (expected / obtained) results
Explanation of the (expected / obtained) findings in relation to the original research questions
